      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653",
      "widgets_values": [
        "## R2V: transfer by reference\n\nHere the images do not become frames. The model takes a **character, a style,\nan object** out of them and carries it into a new scene that you describe in\nthe prompt.\n\n`ref_image_size` = 2048 on the short side: references are read at a higher\nresolution than the output video so there is enough detail to work with.\n\nYou can pass several references, and also video and audio through the\n`ref_videos` and `ref_audios` slots. An audio reference sets the voice or the\nmusical character.\n\n**Turbo needs a note here.** R2V loads a different checkpoint (`ref2va` instead\nof `fl2va`), and the LoRA author only claims t2v and i2v as verified. I ran it:\nthe LoRA bound completely, all 208 backbone modules plus 51 adaln, and a\n608x352 clip came out clean with the composition and the character intact. So\nthe keys match here too.\n\nI tested on throwaway images though, not on a real character transfer job. How\nwell identity holds at four steps is worth checking with your own references.\nIf it falls apart, going back to 20 steps is described in the turbo card.\n"
      ]
    }
